[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Eurobot System Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @eurobot

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
System (black box) requirements. Each requirement declares a ``COVERS``
relation to every ``RULE`` it addresses.

These four requirements cover three clauses out of the 93 that
``Eurobot_Rules.sdoc`` holds, so the Traceability Matrix shows a long list
of rules nobody has written a requirement for yet. Working that list down
is the course's own job.

The rules are in Russian and the requirements are in English, because the
rules are quoted from the competition documents while the requirements are
the course's own writing.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-1
TITLE: Footprint at the start of a match
TARGET_REVISION: C1
STATEMENT: >>>
At the start of a match, the robot shall fit inside a perimeter of at most
1200 mm, measured around the convex hull of its vertical projection on the
ground.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-GENERAL-F.3
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-2
TITLE: Height during a match
TARGET_REVISION: C1
STATEMENT: >>>
At any time during a match, the robot shall measure at most 350 mm from the
table surface to its highest point. The beacon support mast, and the sensors
and circuits mounted under it, are outside that measurement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-GENERAL-F.3
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-3
TITLE: Emergency stop cuts actuator power
TARGET_REVISION: C2
STATEMENT: >>>
Pressing the emergency stop button shall remove power from every motor and
every actuator within 100 ms, and the robot shall stay unpowered until the
button is released.

The button shall sit on top of the robot or on a side a referee can reach
without moving anything else.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-GENERAL-F.4.c
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-4
TITLE: Autonomous match cycle
TARGET_REVISION: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
After the referee's start signal, the robot shall run its match strategy for
100 seconds and shall stop all motion at the end of that time. It shall take
no input from the team while the match runs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-GENERAL-H.2
  ROLE: COVERS
